WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:07.319
We've mentioned earlier this week this recent
Fox news poll, which has been an absolute

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:09.960
treasure trove of interesting public opinion.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:16.340
And one of the things that it found is that
54% of the country wants Donald Trump impeached.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.360
50% wants Trump impeached and removed from
office.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.789
On yesterday's show, I had video from Fox
and friends where Brian Kilmeade was stunned.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:32.369
His word, not mine, that their own poll found
that half the country wants Donald Trump removed.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.290
Now another one of the really interesting
things in this Fox news poll was the section

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:40.880
with policy questions where it asked, for
example, what do you think of Elizabeth Warren's

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.160
wealth tax?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.210
What do you think about Donald Trump's us
Mexico border wall?

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.660
What do you think about Medicare for all?

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.880
And the Fox news poll found that the wealth
tax is way more popular with Americans than

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.750
Donald Trump's border wall.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.200
68% of the country supports Elizabeth Warren's
wealth tax.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.210
Only 44% of Americans support Donald Trump's
border wall.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:08.220
The wealth tax is roughly 50% more popular
than the border wall.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.040
55 ish percent more popular.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:17.069
If you give people a choice between let's
tax really rich people or let's build a wall

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:22.060
on the us Mexico border, way more people want
to tax rich people then want to build this

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.060
wall.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:29.009
The uh, uh, the, the, the sort of incongruency
is that if you look at media coverage, especially

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:33.859
on right wing media, they treat the wealth
tax like this absurd.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:40.079
Supposedly socialist pipe dream while the
wall is treated as it's correct, it's obvious,

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:45.700
it's pragmatic, it's effective, it's just
a matter of getting Democrats to allow Donald

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.219
Trump the money he needs to build the wall.

00:01:48.219 --> 00:01:55.349
So it's really important to understand that
media coverage of policy proposals and ideas

00:01:55.349 --> 00:02:00.400
is not reflective number one of public opinion
about those policies, ideas of those policy

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:06.520
ideas and number two of the degree to which
the policies are feasible.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.390
Uh, now it's important to also notice, I want
to be totally transparent here because I know

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.670
people will say, David, you've got to talk
about the results in the poll about Medicare

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.350
for all the same poll shows.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:22.140
Medicare for all as described in the poll
is not that popular.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.400
There's a question in this Fox news poll about
replacing the private health insurance system

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.500
that we have with a government run program.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.900
It has only 41% support.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:38.490
Now we know from experience that the wording
on that question really influences what people

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.490
say.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:44.530
So on the one hand you can almost guarantee
low support for Medicare for all type system.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.670
If you say something like, do you support
a government takeover of healthcare?

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.570
That wording will get a low level of support.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:55.570
On the other hand, you can get off high level
of support for Medicare for all, if you phrase

00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:00.510
it as should the government provide a basic
level of care to everyone regardless of ability

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.700
to pay, even though that's not exactly what
Medicare for all is, but the point is the

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.200
wording of these healthcare questions really
influenced the support.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:14.960
Now, that being said, I want to tell everyone,
Fox news polls are considered pretty solid.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.730
They are rated a by a number of different
organizations that rate pollsters including

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:23.800
five 38 this says nothing about Fox news TV
channel.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.420
It says nothing about the content of Fox news
radio.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:32.390
Their polling is considered relatively good
polling, so I do think we need to accept when

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.090
they say 68% favor a wealth tax, it's probably
close to that.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:42.410
When they say only 41% support replacing private
insurance with a government run plant run

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.830
plan, it's probably close to that.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.910
That doesn't mean that the question is asked
in the way that most clearly explains what

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.430
it is that's being proposed.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.050
But that's part of the problem.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:57.530
Part of the problem is the messaging and that
people don't understand what it is that's

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.530
being proposed.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:03.430
It also, by the way, doesn't mean that a government
run program is bad.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:09.740
All the poll tells us is that there's a long
way to go in garnering more public support.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:14.450
And much of that lack of support certainly
comes from a lack of understanding of what

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:19.359
the proposals are and because of successful
smear campaigns against these programs.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:24.889
But my message to you today is, unless we
recognize that we have a lot of work to do

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:30.159
to make Medicare for all more popular with
the public, we're going to have trouble implementing

00:04:30.159 --> 00:04:31.159
it.

00:04:31.159 --> 00:04:36.120
And by the way, I mean what, you know, the,
uh, the Obama era and the failure, despite

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.020
overwhelming public support to pass universal
background checks for firearm purchases, we

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.599
know that even with overwhelming public support,
it can be very difficult to actually make

00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:47.310
policy happen and make things happen.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.960
So it's an uphill battle.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.289
It's a worthwhile one.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:55.909
But in the meantime, uh, significantly more
support for Elizabeth Warren's wealth tax

00:04:55.909 --> 00:05:00.720
than for Donald Trump's wall based on Fox
news, his own poll.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.659
You won't hear much discussion of that on
Fox news as airwaves, but I encourage you

00:05:04.659 --> 00:05:08.520
to look at the poll and look at these issue
by issue questions because the results are

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.469
very, very interesting.

00:05:10.469 --> 00:05:15.499
Make sure you're following the David Pakman
show on Instagram at David Pakman show.

00:05:15.499 --> 00:05:19.129
While you're there, follow me at David dot
Pacman.

